From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 18:07:37 +0800
Subject: screen-cast: Run monitor MemFd capture immediately after input

Monitor streams using MemFd record frames in a detached paint scheduled from
stage_painted().  g_idle_add() uses G_PRIORITY_DEFAULT_IDLE, so ordinary main
loop sources can starve that recording callback for hundreds of milliseconds.

The previous UU Remote candidate scheduled the same one-shot callback after a
1 ms delay at CLUTTER_PRIORITY_REDRAW + 1.  That prevents capture from
overtaking a redraw, but a continuously ready redraw source can keep the
coalesced callback pending and make the visible stream lag behind IME edits.

Mutter's own priority design notes in src/meta/common.h say work that should
happen immediately must use G_PRIORITY_DEFAULT, and warn that sources below
redraw can be delayed arbitrarily while the screen updates rapidly.  Run the
delayed callback at G_PRIORITY_DEFAULT.  It is created only after
stage_painted() has completed, so it cannot overtake the paint that created
it; once its 1 ms timeout becomes ready, it can be dispatched with the other
default-priority ready sources instead of being starved by redraw.  This
retains the existing one-shot, coalescing, and lifetime behavior.

---
 src/backends/meta-screen-cast-monitor-stream-src.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/meta-screen-cast-monitor-stream-src.c b/src/backends/meta-screen-cast-monitor-stream-src.c
index b13b25d..8cd689e 100644
--- a/src/backends/meta-screen-cast-monitor-stream-src.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-screen-cast-monitor-stream-src.c
@@ -184,8 +184,12 @@ stage_painted (MetaStage        *stage,
 
   if (!(record_result & META_SCREEN_CAST_RECORD_RESULT_RECORDED_FRAME))
     {
-      monitor_src->maybe_record_idle_id = g_idle_add (maybe_record_frame_on_idle,
-                                                      src);
+      monitor_src->maybe_record_idle_id =
+        g_timeout_add_full (G_PRIORITY_DEFAULT,
+                            1,
+                            maybe_record_frame_on_idle,
+                            src,
+                            NULL);
       g_source_set_name_by_id (monitor_src->maybe_record_idle_id,
                                "[mutter] maybe_record_frame_on_idle [monitor-src]");
     }
